ally renamed this one section to the plural \"searchComponents\" in the URL;","+  public void testGetConfigComponentByNameOnListSectionReturnsNotFound() {","+    // List-shaped sections are excluded from the by-name @Path; Jersey should return 404.","+    for (String component :","+        List.of(\"listeners\", \"initParams\", \"updateRequestProcessorChain\", \"circuitBreaker\")) {","+      var request =","+          new ConfigApi.GetConfigComponentByName(IndexType.CORE, CORE_NAME, component, \"random\");","+      final RemoteSolrException ex =","+          expectThrows(","+              RemoteSolrException.class,","+              () -> request.process(solrTestRule.getSolrClient(CORE_NAME)));","+      assertEquals(404, ex.code());","+    }","+  }","+","+  @Test","+  public void testGetConfigComponentRejectsOldSingularPaths() {","+    // v2-only plurals;","     // the old singular form (still used by v1) shouldn't match the v2 route at all.","-    var request = new ConfigApi.GetConfigComponent(IndexType.CORE, CORE_NAME, \"searchComponent\");","-    final RemoteSolrException ex =","-        expectThrows(","-            RemoteSolrException.class,","-            () -> request.process(solrTestRule.getSolrClient(CORE_NAME)));","-    assertEquals(404, ex.code());","+    for (String component :","+        List.of(","+            \"searchComponent\",","+            \"queryResponseWriter\",","+            \"listener\",","+            \"queryParser\",","+            \"valueSourceParser\",","+            \"transformer\",","+            \"updateProcessor\",","+            \"queryConverter\",","+            \"expressible\",","+            \"cache\")) {","+      var request = new ConfigApi.GetConfigComponent(IndexType.CORE, CORE_NAME, component);","+      final RemoteSolrException ex =","+          expectThrows(","+              RemoteSolrException.class,","+              () -> request.process(solrTestRule.getSolrClient(CORE_NAME)));","+      assertEquals(404, ex.code());","+    }","   }"," }"],"additions":68,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"solr/solr-ref-guide/modules/configuration-guide/pages/config-api.adoc","lines":["@@ -124,8 +124,12 @@ The output will be details of each request handler defined in `solrconfig.xml`,"," To see the configuration for implicit request handlers, add `expandParams=true` to the request."," See the documentation for implicit request handlers linked above for examples using this command."," ","-The available top-level sections that can be added as path parameters are: `query`, `requestHandler`, `searchComponent`, `updateHandler`, `queryResponseWriter`, `initParams`, `znodeVersion`, `listener`, `directoryFactory`, `indexConfig`, and `codecFactory`.","-In the V2 API, `requestHandler`, `searchComponent` and `queryResponseWriter` are exposed under the pluralized names `requestHandlers`, `searchComponents` and `queryResponseWriters` instead (including the response JSON key).","+The available top-level sections that can be added as path parameters include: `query`, `requestHandler`, `searchComponent`, `updateHandler`, `queryResponseWriter`, `initParams`, `znodeVersion`, `listener`, `directoryFactory`, `indexConfig`, and `codecFactory`.","+(Other `solrconfig.xml` sections emitted by Solr may also be fetched the same way)","+","+In the V2 API, several multi-valued sections use pluralized path names (and the same plural as the response JSON key).","+","+V1 paths keep the singular / internal names unchanged."," "," To further restrict the request to a single component within a top-level section, use the `componentName` request parameter."," ","@@ -166,9 +170,10 @@ The output of this command will look similar to(V1 nests under `requestHandler`;"," }"," ----"," ","-The ability to restrict to objects within a top-level section is limited to request handlers (`requestHandler`), search components (`searchComponent`), and response writers (`queryResponseWriter`).","+By-name lookup applies to sections that are maps of named plugins, such as request handlers, search components, response writers etc.","+List-shaped sections like initParams, listeners, updateRequestProcessorChain etc cannot be filtered by name."," ","-For search components and response writers, the V2 API uses a path segment instead of the `componentName` request parameter, under the pluralized section names.","+For those name-keyed sections other than the request handler, the V2 API uses a path segment instead of the `componentName` request parameter, under the pluralized section names."," For example, to return configuration for the `elevator` search component:"," "," [tabs#getnamedcomponent]","@@ -191,7 +196,7 @@ http://localhost:8983/api/collections/techproducts/config/searchComponents/eleva"," ===="," ======"," ","-The same applies to response writers.","+The same pattern applies to other named-key sections."," For example, to return configuration for the `xslt` response writer:"," "," [tabs#getnamedwriter]","@@ -202,6 +207,7 @@ V1 API::"," [source,bash]"," ----"," http://localhost:8983/solr/techproducts/config/queryResponseWriter?componentName=xslt","+http://localhost:8983/solr/techproducts/config/updateProcessor?componentName=uuid"," ----"," ===="," V2 API::","@@ -210,11 +216,12 @@ V2 API::"," [source,bash]"," ----"," http://localhost:8983/api/collections/techproducts/config/queryResponseWriters/xslt","+http://localhost:8983/api/collections/techproducts/config/updateProcessors/uuid"," ----"," ===="," ======"," ","-Request handlers are unaffected and continue to use `componentName` in both APIs, as shown above.","+Request handlers are a special case and continue to use `componentName` in both APIs, as shown above."," "," == Commands to Modify the Config"," ",""],"additions":13,"deletions":6,"truncated":false}],"additions":148,"deletions":85,"truncated":false,"file_count":8},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-10-21T13:28:45.333284+00:00"}